        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: mobile operator terminal (iOS) with full-screen web terminal view",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOperators cannot use the Gateway terminal from a phone. The web Control UI ships a dockable ghostty-web terminal (PTY protocol + reattach already on `main`), but there was no mobile surface for it: the Control UI always renders the full shell chrome, and the iOS app had no terminal destination.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nInstead of reimplementing a terminal natively, the iOS app embeds the existing gateway-served web terminal in a thin WKWebView host. This PR adds the two pieces that make that possible:\n\n- **Control UI**: a full-screen, terminal-only document mode at `/?view=terminal`. `<openclaw-terminal-panel>` gains a `fullscreen` property (viewport-filling, always open while available, no dock/resize chrome, auto-opens its first session, and keeps the panel alive after the last tab closes since there is no toggle to bring it back). `app-host.ts` renders just the terminal panel (plus an unavailable notice) for this mode. Composes with the shipped reattach flow: fullscreen documents reattach persisted sessions on reconnect exactly like the docked panel.\n- **iOS**: a `TerminalHubScreen` Control-hub sidebar destination (`.terminal`, no 6th tab — iOS is at the 5-tab limit) hosting a `WKWebView` pointed at `/?view=terminal` on the active gateway. Credentials are injected via an origin-gated document-start `WKUserScript` using the existing `__OPENCLAW_NATIVE_CONTROL_AUTH__` startup contract (same mechanism as the macOS Dashboard window) — the token never appears in the page URL, WebKit history, or gateway request logs. Ephemeral website data store; the web view is recreated only when the gateway endpoint/credentials change so SwiftUI update passes never restart live shells.\n\nNo gateway protocol changes; purely additive on the shipped `terminal.*` surface.\n\n## User Impact\n\niOS operators get a Terminal entry in the Control hub: a full-screen shell in the agent workspace, with the same session reattach behavior as the desktop Control UI (background the app, come back, sessions survive within the detach grace period). Availability follows the existing gate (`gateway.terminal.enabled` + `operator.admin` + advertised `terminal.open`); a clear notice is shown otherwise. Docs: Control UI operator-terminal section documents the `?view=terminal` mode.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Web: full UI vitest project green (120 files / 1942 tests, including a new fullscreen regression test in `ui/src/components/terminal/terminal-panel.test.ts`), `pnpm tsgo` + `pnpm check:test-types` green, directory-scan oxlint (`node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.core.json src ui packages`) clean, `pnpm ui:i18n:sync` regenerated bundles/metadata.\n- iOS: `xcodebuild` device build (generic/platform=iOS) succeeded; full OpenClaw scheme test run on iPhone 17 Pro simulator passed, including new `TerminalHubScreenTests` (URL derivation keeps credentials out of the URL; auth user script origin-gated; no script without credentials); swiftformat + swiftlint clean.\n- Functional proof (screenshots in comments): terminal-only view served by a dev gateway from this branch, opened in the iOS environment, shell command executed.\n- Real-device note: no paired iOS device was available during verification (the only wired device is unpaired); simulator proof + device build provided, device smoke to follow when hardware is reachable.\n",
